1. Challenge Overview
This challenge focused on recognizing and decoding multiple layers of encoded information. I downloaded the provided challenge file, identified Base64-encoded data, decoded more than one Base64 layer, and then recognized that the remaining text used a Caesar cipher. I used a Caesar cipher solver to test the shift and confirm the readable result.
The main lesson from this challenge was that one successful decode does not always mean the investigation is finished. An analyst still has to inspect the new output, identify what type of data it is, and decide what technique should be used next.

