4. Investigation Procedure 

Step 1 — Download the Challenge File
I used wget in the CyLab webshell to download the file provided by the challenge.
wget "<challenge-file-url>" -O enc_flag
Result: The download completed successfully and the file was saved as enc_flag.


Step 2 — Identify and Decode the Base64 Layers
After opening the file, I found a long string that matched the common appearance of Base64 data. I copied the encoded value into the EMN178 Base64 Decode tool.
The first decode did not produce normal plaintext. Instead, it produced another Base64-looking value. I decoded that second layer as well.
Sanitized decoded-content:
First decode: another Base64-encoded value
Second decode: Caesar-cipher text

Step 3 — Solve the Caesar Cipher
The second Base64 decode produced text that was readable in structure but still had shifted letters. That was a clue that the next layer was a Caesar cipher.
I copied only the ciphertext into The Word Finder Caesar Cipher Solver and tested the shift values until the text became readable and matched the expected challenge flag format.
